From ff33b8e8c98ff0332ae1357db628721ea8726fef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:25:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] Chat with the professionals from the app

Tapping a professional on the follow-up card opens the conversation of
that follow-up: the messages oldest first (newest at the bottom), photos
downloaded with the login from the attachment endpoint, videos named as
such, and a field to send a text while the follow-up is open (an ended one
keeps the history). Opening the conversation marks the professional's
unread messages as read. A failed send keeps the text and says so.

The answer of the server is decoded as UTF-8 explicitly: DRF sends JSON
without a charset, and the default Latin-1 decoding broke accents.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
